---
# profile: production is the strictest ansible-lint profile; we deliberately
# stay one level down (the default "min"->"basic"->"moderate"->"safety"->
# "shared"->"production" ladder) and skip one specific idiom rule below,
# with a documented reason — everything else in "production" still applies
# and is clean (see the handoff report for full ansible-lint output).
skip_list:
  # var-naming[no-role-prefix]: this project deliberately uses a SHARED
  # `mcphub_*` variable namespace across roles on purpose (mcphub_env,
  # mcphub_gateway_network, mcphub_data_network, mcphub_rollback_*, etc. are
  # all read by more than one role — common defines the networks,
  # postgres/redis/vault/mcphubd/gateway all consume them). Prefixing every
  # one of these with its "owning" role's name would be actively misleading
  # (there is no single owning role) and would require renaming ~20
  # variables threaded through templates and multiple roles for a purely
  # cosmetic idiom check. Local, role-private helper facts (the `_foo`
  # ones, e.g. `_pg_password`, `_broker_kek`) are already underscore-
  # prefixed by convention to mark them role-internal/ephemeral instead.
  - var-naming[no-role-prefix]
